Note case 3: the object comes from an external file outside the project root, yet it lands in the current package output as `[dbo].[Table2]` — external_sql_files + build means full schema compilation for that file. Contrast that with feature4, where referenced-project objects never appear. Don't conflate the two mechanisms.

Two artifacts, verbatim. Ground truth.

feature4_reference_resolution:
{
  "description": "Resolve dependencies from referenced database projects and report that schema objects depending on referenced objects compile into the requesting project package.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "sql_files": {
          "View1.sql": "-- This view references Table1 which is created in the referenced project\nCREATE VIEW [dbo].[View1]\n  AS SELECT * FROM [Table1]\n"
        },
        "project_references": [
          {
            "path": "/external/ReferenceProj/ReferenceProj.sqlproj",
            "sql_files": {
              "Table1.sql": "CREATE TABLE [dbo].[Table1]\n(\n\tc1 int NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,\n\tc2 int NULL\n)\n"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": "exit_code=0\npackage_exists=true\ntables=\nviews=[dbo].[View1]\npre_deploy_script=false\npost_deploy_script=false\ndiagnostics=none\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "sql_files": {
          "View1.sql": "-- This view references Table1 which is created in the referenced project\nCREATE VIEW [dbo].[View1]\n  AS SELECT * FROM [Table1]\n"
        },
        "nested_project_references": [
          {
            "path": "ReferenceProj/ReferenceProj.sqlproj",
            "sql_files": {
              "Table1.sql": "CREATE TABLE [dbo].[Table1]\n(\n\tc1 int NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,\n\tc2 int NULL\n)\n"
            }
          }
        ],
        "project_reference_paths": [
          "ReferenceProj/ReferenceProj.sqlproj"
        ],
        "remove_build": [
          "ReferenceProj/**/*.*"
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": "exit_code=0\npackage_exists=true\ntables=\nviews=[dbo].[View1]\npre_deploy_script=false\npost_deploy_script=false\ndiagnostics=none\n"
    }
  ]
}

feature5_unresolved_reference_diagnostics:
{
  "description": "Reject a database project whose schema references an object that is not supplied by the project or its references, and report a normalized unresolved-reference diagnostic.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "sql_files": {
          "Table1.sql": "CREATE TABLE [dbo].[Table1]\n(\n\tc1 int NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,\n\tc2 int NULL\n)\n",
          "View2.sql": "-- This view references Table2 which does not exist\nCREATE VIEW [dbo].[View2]\n  AS SELECT * FROM [Table2]\n"
        }
      },
      "expected_output": "exit_code=1\npackage_exists=false\ntables=\nviews=\npre_deploy_script=false\npost_deploy_script=false\ndiagnostics=error_code=SQL71501;object=[dbo].[View2];referenced=[dbo].[Table2]\n"
    }
  ]
}

Note the nested case in feature4: `project_reference_paths` and the `remove_build` glob appear together with `nested_project_references` — that combination is required, not optional. And in feature5, note `[Table2]` referenced unqualified in the view body still renders as `[dbo].[Table2]` in the diagnostic. You now hold all five public artifacts. That's every card I show.
